   },
   "source": [
    "## Our first program: GC content\n",
    "\n",
    "This opening example is biologically meaningful and compact.\n",
    "\n",
    "It demonstrates:\n",
    "- function definition\n",
    "- variables\n",
    "- a loop over a sequence\n",
    "- a conditional statement\n",
    "- a return value\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "dca80c03",
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "subslide"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def GC_content(dna_string):\n",
    "    ''' calculate %GC in dna_string (uppercase ACTG) '''\n",
    "    GC = 0\n",
    "    for nuc in dna_string: # iterate over dna_string\n",
    "        if nuc == \"C\" or nuc == \"G\":\n",
    "            GC += 1 # equal to GC = GC+1\n",
    "    return 100*GC/len(dna_string)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "1ce14234",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      " calculate %GC in dna_string (uppercase ACTG) \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(GC_content.__doc__)"
   ]
  },
